THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
SRC_002 proposes materializing each reinstatement step as an explicit inference edge with its own warrant inside the witness, making the derived reinstatement property per-step auditable. The problem requires preserving 'reinstatement as a derived property.' Once reinstatement steps are explicit inference edges carrying their own warrants, reinstatement is no longer derived from the grounded fixed-point semantics; it is reified as a first-class object in the witness structure. An explicit edge with its own warrant is an independent assertion of reinstatement, not a derivation of it. The proposal claims 'the derivation remains,' but materializing the step as an inspectable edge with its own warrant changes reinstatement from a consequence of the semantics into a stored artifact, violating the requirement that it stay a derived property.

TARGET:
Challenge reinstatement-as-derived by materializing each reinstatement step as an explicit inference edge carrying its own warrant inside the witness, turning the derived property into an inspectable chain while still proving the final labels coincide with the grounded fixpoint — the derivation remains but becomes per-step auditable, and the committed-root validity guarantee must be re-verified against the explicit edges.